for us, we also get to see the other side of the coin of what sin actually does in our lives.

00:15:15.360 --> 00:15:19.440
And so I want us to dig in there a little bit. As much as it's not fun to talk about sin,

00:15:19.440 --> 00:15:24.100
it's important because if we don't talk about the reality of sin, we're not going to really

00:15:24.100 --> 00:15:29.100
understand and appreciate what it is that Jesus has done for us. So specifically, if we just take

00:15:29.100 --> 00:15:34.000
the flip side of this coin, we can understand in this passage that what sin does is it makes us

00:15:34.000 --> 00:15:41.840
guilty and enslaved. That's what sin does. And let's dig into that a little bit. When I say sin

00:15:41.840 --> 00:15:47.720
makes us guilty and enslaved, I'm referring to the spiritual effect of sin on our lives.

00:15:47.720 --> 00:15:52.820
I also don't want us to forget that we're not merely victims of sin, but we're perpetrators of

00:15:52.820 --> 00:15:57.900
sin. Sin is not just something we're victims of, and we're just kind of passively, oh, sin happens

00:15:57.900 --> 00:16:04.680
to me. No, we sin. We do things that are against God's will. We rebel against his revealed word,

00:16:04.760 --> 00:16:09.320
his command. We do things that offend his honor and glory. We do things that sin against one

00:16:09.320 --> 00:16:16.240
another as well. We all do that. The effect of that on our lives is that we become guilty and

00:16:16.240 --> 00:16:21.080
enslaved. And so think about this here. Paul, as he's writing this letter to the church in Ephesus,

00:16:21.480 --> 00:16:26.800
he's not coming up with these as like new ideas out of nowhere. He, in all of this, he's referring

00:16:26.800 --> 00:16:32.780
back to the Old Testament that the Jewish people had known for centuries at this point. And he's

00:16:32.780 --> 00:16:39.060
thinking probably about things like Proverbs 5.22. It says, the iniquities of the wicked ensnare him,

00:16:39.060 --> 00:16:45.620
and he is held fast in the cords of sin. So he's saying when we fall into sin, we actually

00:16:45.620 --> 00:16:50.580
become ensnared by it, trapped by it, unable to get out of it. If I could describe like what that

00:16:50.580 --> 00:16:56.100
might actually look like just in a very simple example, like just imagine that a person has

00:16:56.100 --> 00:17:01.500
been dishonest about a seemingly small matter. Maybe they told what they thought was a little

00:17:01.500 --> 00:17:07.620
white lie to get out of the consequences of something, okay? So maybe like, oh, did you,

00:17:08.080 --> 00:17:13.920
you know, maybe something like, did you leave the toilet seat up? No, I didn't do that.

00:17:14.700 --> 00:17:16.420
Somebody else must have come along and done that.

00:17:16.500 --> 00:17:18.240
Okay, well, it seems like a little white lie

00:17:18.240 --> 00:17:21.580
to get out of being in trouble for not putting the toilet seat down.

00:17:21.840 --> 00:17:22.740
It seems small.

00:17:23.280 --> 00:17:26.680
But now imagine, somebody else comes along and says,

00:17:27.140 --> 00:17:28.880
well, no one else has gone in and out of that bathroom.

00:17:30.720 --> 00:17:33.060
Maybe now that person's kind of stuck.

00:17:33.820 --> 00:17:36.100
Now, okay, I need to come up with another lie

00:17:36.100 --> 00:17:37.820
to cover up my previous lie

00:17:37.820 --> 00:17:39.600
if I don't want to take responsibility for it.

00:17:40.100 --> 00:17:41.340
And so I come up with something of like,

00:17:41.340 --> 00:17:44.160
oh, maybe the dog went in there and did it.

00:17:45.260 --> 00:17:48.360
And then someone says, oh, but the dog's been outside for the last two hours.

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:48.900
Oh, God.

00:17:49.920 --> 00:17:50.920
Maybe the cat did.

00:17:51.000 --> 00:17:51.500
I don't know.

00:17:51.660 --> 00:17:57.160
Like, you see, people start coming up with lies to maintain lies.

00:17:57.500 --> 00:17:59.940
And the further you go down that path,

00:18:00.300 --> 00:18:03.360
now significant relationships are on the line.

00:18:03.740 --> 00:18:06.640
And a person's reputation in front of others are on the line.

00:18:06.640 --> 00:18:24.580
And this becomes a snare wrapped around a person that started with just a small seed of seemingly meaningless dishonesty that now has ensnared that person where now they have to keep that lie going and try to use deception to avoid responsibility and save face.

00:18:24.840 --> 00:18:26.060
And that becomes habitual.

00:18:27.160 --> 00:18:29.500
It becomes the way we live.

00:18:30.080 --> 00:18:31.920
And you can apply that to anything, right?

00:18:31.940 --> 00:18:34.000
I'm just using a very small, simple example.

00:18:34.560 --> 00:18:39.280
How much more powerful is that snare, that enslavement,

00:18:39.800 --> 00:18:42.340
when it deals with things that are of heavier weight

00:18:42.340 --> 00:18:46.460
and their impact on our lives and on those around us?

