00:50:52.340 --> 00:50:57.840
briefly, I remember I had to learn this lesson the hard way because I, like everybody else, grew up,

00:50:57.940 --> 00:51:02.420
this is the way you do it. You hide, you justify, you pretend, you try to avoid it. But I remember

00:51:02.420 --> 00:51:06.700
like probably roughly 20 years ago or so, I was here in our church. I've been following Jesus for

00:51:06.700 --> 00:51:11.420
a few years, thought I knew the right answers. But I was here, I was serving, I was serving as a leader

00:51:11.420 --> 00:51:16.320
in our church. By the way, having a leadership title doesn't mean you're not sinning, just FYI.

00:51:17.940 --> 00:51:23.120
and I was serving in leadership, and there was another person serving in leadership,

00:51:23.460 --> 00:51:30.180
and I didn't like some of the decisions he was making, ways he was leading, stuff like that,

00:51:30.280 --> 00:51:35.080
and I was not in a good place spiritually, I don't think. Again, like, being a leader doesn't mean

00:51:35.080 --> 00:51:39.680
you're not struggling spiritually, and out of that, there was just this bitterness in my heart,

00:51:39.760 --> 00:51:44.240
this judgment in my heart, and I started, I was just, like, getting really angry at this other

00:51:44.240 --> 00:51:49.140
person serving in leadership, and I was, I would, and I knew I shouldn't, like, do anything really

00:51:49.140 --> 00:51:54.000
outwardly, but what I would do is, like, I would, you know, kind of say passive-aggressive comments

00:51:54.000 --> 00:51:59.760
to him, and, like, to him or about him in meetings that we were having. I would, like, go and, like,

00:51:59.760 --> 00:52:03.340
tell somebody else, like, man, you see what that decision that guy made, like, it's a stupid

00:52:03.340 --> 00:52:09.080
decision, like, I would, and I would do everything but directly confront the issue, and in doing

00:52:09.080 --> 00:52:16.340
that, eventually, somebody came to me and said, Pete, what are you doing? What's wrong? And I had

00:52:16.340 --> 00:52:21.080
to realize this sin in my heart that I somehow thought I was better than. I somehow thought

00:52:21.080 --> 00:52:26.540
that this other person was so much worse than me. And instead of dealing with that in a way, like,

00:52:27.620 --> 00:52:33.440
lavished with the grace of God like we can do, instead, I was doing that passive aggressively,

00:52:33.900 --> 00:52:38.280
critically, condemning him, tearing him down. I was doing all that stuff. And it wasn't until a

00:52:38.280 --> 00:52:42.440
brother came along and confronted me and said, Pete, what you're doing is not right. This is not

00:52:42.440 --> 00:52:47.580
how you live in the grace and mercy of God. And he challenged me, and I realized I had to go to that

00:52:47.580 --> 00:52:52.220
brother. I had to confess to him. I had to say, hey, I apologize. I've been critical and judgmental

00:52:52.220 --> 00:52:58.500
toward you. Will you forgive me? And you know what? That brother forgave me. We were to love each

00:52:58.500 --> 00:53:03.320
other, care for each other, be friends with each other, because the grace of God covered that. I

00:53:03.320 --> 00:53:04.760
I had to learn that the hard way.

00:53:05.300 --> 00:53:08.200
My fear is that we can come here,

00:53:08.260 --> 00:53:09.700
we can do the things we do on Sunday

00:53:09.700 --> 00:53:10.820
in our life groups, all that.

00:53:10.900 --> 00:53:12.760
We can serve, we can do all the stuff that we do.

00:53:13.200 --> 00:53:14.260
And behind the scenes,

00:53:15.700 --> 00:53:17.100
where we're actually living our relationship

00:53:17.100 --> 00:53:19.460
with God and others is just rotten with sin.

00:53:20.580 --> 00:53:22.140
So how do you deal with that?

00:53:22.840 --> 00:53:25.040
And by the way, I just want to give an invitation here today.

00:53:25.140 --> 00:53:25.620
There are some of you,

00:53:25.680 --> 00:53:27.380
maybe you are checking out the Christian faith.

00:53:28.060 --> 00:53:29.480
Maybe you know the weight

00:53:29.480 --> 00:53:31.580
of trying to deal with your own sin

00:53:31.580 --> 00:53:33.060
and maybe you've known it for a long time.

00:53:33.960 --> 00:53:35.020
You've been trying to hide.

00:53:35.720 --> 00:53:38.080
You've been trying to pay the price yourself.

00:53:38.700 --> 00:53:41.240
I'm trying to pretend it isn't enslaving you

00:53:41.240 --> 00:53:42.480
when you really know that it is.

00:53:42.900 --> 00:53:45.880
Can I invite you today to be in Christ with us?

00:53:46.800 --> 00:53:48.340
It's not that this is a perfect community,

00:53:48.980 --> 00:53:51.900
but we follow a Savior who has given his life for us.

00:53:52.420 --> 00:53:53.700
He shed his blood on the cross,

00:53:53.700 --> 00:53:55.780
not just for the person sitting next to you, but for you.

00:53:56.460 --> 00:53:58.540
And today I want you to be in Christ,

00:53:59.080 --> 00:54:02.360
meaning that you trust his sacrifice for you,

00:54:02.360 --> 00:54:04.920
that through the blood he shed on the cross,

00:54:05.040 --> 00:54:06.500
he has set you free from slavery

00:54:06.500 --> 00:54:08.140
and he's set you free from guilt.

00:54:08.400 --> 00:54:09.060
It's atoned for.

00:54:09.660 --> 00:54:11.140
Can you pray to him today?

00:54:11.260 --> 00:54:12.040
Trust in him today.

00:54:12.160 --> 00:54:15.260
Say, I'm placing my faith in Jesus as my savior today.

00:54:15.340 --> 00:54:17.980
I wanna follow him and live in his grace today.

00:54:18.240 --> 00:54:19.400
I would love for you to do that

00:54:19.400 --> 00:54:21.580
even on your own now in your relationship with God,

00:54:21.620 --> 00:54:23.600
but maybe come and talk to one of the prayer team afterward

00:54:23.600 --> 00:54:26.540
and say, hey, I'm choosing to place my faith in Jesus today.

00:54:26.540 --> 00:54:28.700
I wanna give you that invitation this morning.

00:54:29.520 --> 00:54:31.500
As we want to live in that together,

00:54:31.500 --> 00:54:35.160
can I also ask you, are you living in unity with your brothers and sisters in Christ?

00:54:36.640 --> 00:54:44.040
Are you living in unity? Where have things like unforgiveness, comparison, gossip, jealousy,

00:54:44.820 --> 00:54:49.900
simple personality differences, where have these caused division among us? And is there maybe a

00:54:49.900 --> 00:54:54.460
conflict or a conversation you've been avoiding rather than trusting God to redeem and restore?

00:54:55.500 --> 00:54:59.300
And lastly, thirdly, do you trust God to work out his purpose and plan?

00:55:00.240 --> 00:55:01.760
This is kind of getting back to the mystery stuff

00:55:01.760 --> 00:55:02.360
I shared earlier.

00:55:03.240 --> 00:55:06.380
A lot of us, we struggle to really follow and trust God

00:55:06.380 --> 00:55:08.260
because we're like, God, it doesn't make sense to me.

00:55:08.860 --> 00:55:11.100
I don't see the whole roadmap yet.

00:55:11.200 --> 00:55:13.080
Again, I've talked before, God doesn't give you a roadmap,

00:55:13.280 --> 00:55:14.000
God gives you a compass.

00:55:15.700 --> 00:55:17.300
We're like, God, I just can't follow you yet.

00:55:17.300 --> 00:55:19.620
I can't fully trust because I don't know everything.

00:55:20.320 --> 00:55:24.060
Can I ask you today, can you trust that God has a purpose?

00:55:24.280 --> 00:55:25.360
God has a plan.

00:55:25.620 --> 00:55:28.760
It's a plan bigger than you or I could possibly conceive of

00:55:28.760 --> 00:55:31.620
because it's been from before time until the end of time,

00:55:31.720 --> 00:55:33.520
but his plan will be accomplished

00:55:33.520 --> 00:55:34.860
through his son, Jesus Christ.

00:55:35.180 --> 00:55:36.400
Can we believe that today?

00:55:37.260 --> 00:55:39.420
Because when we trust that plan,

00:55:39.980 --> 00:55:41.680
then we can actually rest

00:55:41.680 --> 00:55:44.340
and have peace in our hearts

00:55:44.340 --> 00:55:45.860
even when we don't fully understand.

00:55:47.420 --> 00:55:49.560
And if we trust in that plan,

00:55:50.380 --> 00:55:52.540
then we can actually take steps of faith

00:55:52.540 --> 00:55:53.700
in response to God.

00:55:54.300 --> 00:55:56.260
And even when we can't fully control everything,

00:55:56.540 --> 00:55:57.820
but we can respond to God and say,

00:55:57.820 --> 00:55:59.560
God, I'm gonna take a step of faith today.

00:55:59.940 --> 00:56:01.480
And a lot of times we think, oh, it's a step of faith.

00:56:01.540 --> 00:56:02.920
Yeah, that's serving God in some way.

00:56:02.960 --> 00:56:03.660
That's going on missions.

00:56:04.040 --> 00:56:05.260
Maybe that step of faith today

00:56:05.260 --> 00:56:06.980
is simply confessing your sin to God.

00:56:08.220 --> 00:56:09.200
Saying, God, I can't fix this.

00:56:09.260 --> 00:56:10.580
Maybe that step of faith today is

00:56:10.580 --> 00:56:12.360
I need to reach out to my sister

00:56:12.360 --> 00:56:14.820
because I need to confess something to her.

00:56:16.120 --> 00:56:17.120
Maybe that step of faith is

00:56:17.120 --> 00:56:19.240
I need to place my faith in Jesus for the first time

00:56:19.240 --> 00:56:20.420
even though I can't fully understand.

00:56:21.500 --> 00:56:24.740
Can we trust that God's plans are better than ours

00:56:24.740 --> 00:56:27.160
and then live in that truth together?

00:56:27.820 --> 00:56:29.700
Let's spend some time in response today.

00:56:29.800 --> 00:56:30.840
Can I invite us to stand together?

00:56:44.160 --> 00:56:48.780
As we're standing here, again, I want to just kind of create some space here

00:56:48.780 --> 00:56:51.820
for us personally to respond to God first.

00:56:52.760 --> 00:56:54.080
So just kind of bow your head with me,

00:56:54.200 --> 00:56:59.100
and maybe you want to just reflect through some of those questions I just asked you.

00:57:00.320 --> 00:57:02.200
How am I dealing with the problem of sin?

00:57:03.900 --> 00:57:05.040
Am I living in unity?

00:57:05.160 --> 00:57:08.480
God wants to unite everything in heaven and earth.

00:57:09.100 --> 00:57:10.840
all those warring nations,

00:57:11.160 --> 00:57:13.900
all those tribes that hate one another,

00:57:14.040 --> 00:57:15.700
all those divided relationships,

00:57:16.120 --> 00:57:18.500
everything he wants to bring together in Christ,

00:57:18.820 --> 00:57:21.500
am I simply living in unity with my brothers and sisters?

00:57:24.560 --> 00:57:27.240
Am I trusting that God's plans are better than mine?

00:57:30.610 --> 00:57:32.430
Maybe you want to sit with those questions here

00:57:32.430 --> 00:57:33.570
for a moment before God.

00:57:34.930 --> 00:57:36.990
And as we have this time to respond,

00:57:37.370 --> 00:57:38.290
just as I've shared before,

00:57:38.290 --> 00:57:39.690
we really want this to be like,

00:57:39.730 --> 00:57:41.830
we must seek intimacy with God.

00:57:41.830 --> 00:57:44.490
we must seek fellowship with him

00:57:44.490 --> 00:57:46.050
have the hard conversation

00:57:46.050 --> 00:57:50.050
rest in the truth

00:57:50.050 --> 00:57:52.810
rejoice in the promises

00:57:52.810 --> 00:57:53.990
fulfilled in Christ

00:57:53.990 --> 00:57:56.530
celebrate his

00:57:56.530 --> 00:57:57.450
faithfulness

00:57:57.450 --> 00:58:00.570
mourn the things that have been lost

00:58:00.570 --> 00:58:02.930
be honest

00:58:02.930 --> 00:58:03.750
about the pain

00:58:03.750 --> 00:58:07.940
be honest about the confusion

00:58:07.940 --> 00:58:10.300
bring that to God

00:58:10.300 --> 00:58:12.560
and in relationship with him in this space

00:58:12.560 --> 00:58:14.740
let's believe that he is calling us

00:58:14.740 --> 00:58:19.560
to that higher calling that starts with deep relationship and fellowship with him.

00:58:20.380 --> 00:58:22.660
I'm going to just pray for that for us here for a moment.

00:58:23.360 --> 00:58:27.200
After I pray, we'll just kind of have a short open time just for you to pray and seek the

00:58:27.200 --> 00:58:31.120
Lord, and then the worship team is going to lead us in a couple songs, and let's let

00:58:31.120 --> 00:58:35.240
this be a space to respond to God, to seek him, to say, God, I need to know you.

00:58:35.260 --> 00:58:36.400
I must know you more.

00:58:37.100 --> 00:58:38.860
God, we invite you here again.

00:58:38.860 --> 00:58:43.560
Come, Holy Spirit, work in each and every heart.

00:58:43.560 --> 00:58:47.060
give us the gift of faith and trust

00:58:47.060 --> 00:58:49.900
set us free in this moment

00:58:49.900 --> 00:58:52.660
the power of the blood of Jesus Christ

00:58:52.660 --> 00:58:55.520
sanctify us through and through

00:58:55.520 --> 00:58:58.340
set us free from the things that have been enslaving us

00:58:58.340 --> 00:58:59.400
and bonding us

00:58:59.400 --> 00:59:03.720
wash us clean God of all the guilt and all the shame

00:59:03.720 --> 00:59:07.000
invite us into your great plan

00:59:07.000 --> 00:59:09.780
to know that our lives have a purpose

00:59:09.780 --> 00:59:12.720
to be part of what you're doing until the end of time

00:59:12.720 --> 00:59:14.940
invite us into that Lord

00:59:14.940 --> 00:59:17.060
and especially draw us near Lord

00:59:17.060 --> 00:59:19.020
that we would be close to you

00:59:19.020 --> 00:59:20.600
that we would know you more

00:59:20.600 --> 00:59:22.640
that we would know you so personally

00:59:22.640 --> 00:59:24.240
and intimately in this moment Lord

00:59:24.240 --> 00:59:26.380
come and speak and move

00:59:26.380 --> 00:59:28.980
have your way in us in this space

